# {{alt form|en|short-stop}} {{gloss|to play shortstop}}.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012| title=Nineteenth Century Stars|author=Robert L. Tiemann, Mark Rucker, Joseph M. Overfield | page=20| passage=He captained the Tecumsehs of London, Ontario, (International Association) in 1878; '''shortstopped''' for Cincinnati in 1879; stayed out of baseball in 1880; and finished as shortstop for Boston (NL) in 1881.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2017| title=Playing for a Winner|author=Brandon Isleib | page=77| passage=Managed and '''shortstopped''' by George Wright and full of league stalwarts—Joe Start, Paul Hines, and Jim O'rourke—they also had 1-year-old phenom Monte Ward as primary moundsman (teams now generally used multiple pitchers).}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2017| title=The Sum of Us: Tales of the Bonded and Bound|author=Susan Forest, Lucas K. Law, Juliet Marillier | page=| passage=He '''shortstopped''' for a few years for the Houston Astros when they won the World Series twice in a row. }}
# {{alt form|en|short-stop}} {{gloss|to cause to stop short}}.
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1978|work=Sealift|title=Container Revolution in Bremerhaven|author=Carol D. Jori|volume=|page=18|passage=They will be '''shortstopped''' in the port for lease by the government, then continue their journey by military train. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2006| title=Neodymium Based Ziegler Catalysts - Fundamental Chemistry|author=Oskar Nuyken | page=64| passage=In the polymerization of BD by Ti-, Co- and Ni-based catalyst systems the polymerization has to be '''shortstopped''' at a specific monomer conversion in order to avoid the formation of gel. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2008| title=Phantom Warriors|author=Gary Linderer | page=148| passage=Although he successfully '''shortstopped''' the assault on his two teammates, the enemy soldiers now concentrated their fire directly on him.}}

